\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052{\hich\af6\loch\cf1\fs20\f6\loch
The information you provide is collected under the authority of the }{\hich\af8\loch\cf1\fs20\i\f8\loch
Income Tax Act }{\hich\af6\loch\cf1\fs20\f6\loch
for the purpose of secure transmission of electronic information returns via the Internet. The information will be retained in Personal Information Bank(s) \u8220\'93International and Large Business Income Tax Audit and Examination, }{\hich\af4\loch\cf1\fs20\b\f4\loch
CRA PPU 035 }{\hich\af6\loch\cf1\fs20\f6\loch
" and will be used and disclosed in accordance with the conditions listed therein. Information may also be used for follow-up, audit, compliance, and evaluation purposes and may be shared, in accordance with the Income Tax Act and under existing information-sharing agreements, with other federal institutions and provincial governments. Failure to provide all or parts of the requested information may result in penalties incurred and other non-filer actions.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052{\hich\af6\loch\cf1\fs20\f6\loch
Under the provisions of the Privacy Act, individuals have the right to protection of, and access to, their personal information. For more information about your rights, see www.infosource.gc.ca. This is a Government of Canada publication available in major libraries, at government information offices, and from constituency offices of federal Members of Parliament.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052{\hich\af4\loch\cf1\fs20\b\f4\loch
Confirmation of receipt}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052{\hich\af6\loch\cf1\fs20\f6\loch
Once you file your Corporation Foreign reporting, a preliminary check of your return will be performed. If it meets the basic requirements, CRA will send you a confirmation number within seconds. This means that your return has been accepted for processing. If there are any problems with the electronic return you tried to send to the CRA, you will be prompted with an explanation of error(s) that requires corrections. This means that your return was not accepted by the CRA for processing. You can change the electronic version of your return and then try to send it again using the same Web service.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052{\hich\af6\loch\cf1\fs20\f6\loch
If your return has been accepted for processing, do not submit a paper copy by mail. After CRA has processed your return, we may need to contact you to obtain supporting documents, so remember to keep your documentation for at least six years. This is part of the same verification process that applies to all tax returns, whether paper or electronic.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang4105\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang4105\kerning1\dbch\af9\langfe2052\loch

